# PROPOSED, NOT INSTALLED: needs the user's approval and a BOOT image rebuild
# (docs/EXOCORTEX.md, "Proposed: an init service"). Would go in the boot
# ramdisk's overlay.d beside moon-direct-boot.rc; magiskinit appends it to
# init.rc. Only overlay files change, the ramdisk /init stays the same
# (notes/direct-boot/RESCUE.md).
#
# Android's init then supervises Exocortex's keeper itself: an ordinary
# (not oneshot) service, so init restarts it whenever it exits, in every boot
# mode, and terminates it in its own shutdown sequence. 95-exocortex.sh sees
# init.svc.exocortex running and does nothing; the keeper runs in the
# foreground (`init`): no watchdog, and it stays in this service's cgroup.

service exocortex /system/bin/sh /data/adb/exocortex/exocortex-keeper.sh init
    user root
    group root
    seclabel u:r:magisk:s0
    disabled

# /data (and /data/adb) is mounted and decrypted from post-fs-data on; the
# keeper itself waits for nothing else.
on post-fs-data
    start exocortex

# No stop on moon.boot.mode=shutdown: init's stop kills the whole process
# group at once. moon-power.sh stops the daemon gracefully; the keeper then
# idles until init's shutdown sequence terminates the service.
